  "details": "<p>Excavations in the cave sites identified temporary habitation activities stretching from the Chalcolithic period through to the Roman era. From Roman levels come ca. 120 documents that date to the decades preceding the Bar Kochba revolt of A.D. 132. These texts include documents (deeds, contracts, financial documents) and fragments of Biblical texts.</p>\r\n<p>\u00a0</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Wadi Murabba'at, known also as Nahal Darga, is a ravine in the Judean desert east of Bethlehem. Four cave sites were identified and excavated there in 1952. A fifth cave was identified in 1968.",
